STUDIO HELPER
=============

What this is
-------------
A tool that sets up your print and digital files correctly, names
and organizes everything, and checks your exports before they go to
print or online. It never touches your actual design - only Illustrator,
Photoshop, and Figma do that.


BEFORE YOU EXTRACT THE ZIP
---------------------------
Windows blocks files downloaded from the internet until you tell it
they're OK. Do this once, before you extract:

  1. Right-click the zip file.
  2. Choose Properties.
  3. At the bottom, tick "Unblock", then click OK.
  4. Now extract the zip (right-click -> Extract All...).

If you forget this step, Studio Helper's own Setup check page will
remind you.


STARTING STUDIO HELPER
------------------------
Double-click "Start Studio Helper" inside the extracted folder. Your
browser will open a page - that page IS Studio Helper. You can leave
it open while you work.

The first time you start it, it will show a "Setup check" page that
tells you if Illustrator, Photoshop, Concat and your jobs folder are
ready. Follow any "fix" hints it shows.

It also puts a "Studio Helper" shortcut on your desktop. Use that from
now on: it keeps working after every update. If you delete it, it stays
deleted (Settings -> Desktop shortcut brings it back).

The "?" at the top right opens the Guide: every step, in order.


ONE MASTER, CUT TO EVERY SIZE
-----------------------------
On a job's Files & export tab you can choose "One master, cut to every
size" instead of one artboard per size:

  1. Make the master, in Illustrator (every size, print included) or
     Photoshop (the digital sizes; print stays in Illustrator).
  2. Design everything on it, save, and press "Read the master".
  3. Drag the yellow box around what must stay: headline, logo, offer.
     Every size updates live.
  4. "Cut to every size": the digital files land in 04_export with
     their delivery names; print sizes are placed in your Illustrator
     print file, linked to the master, for Check & export print.

Your master is never changed, and a file you exported yourself is never
replaced without asking.


VIDEOS
------
The Video tab on a job makes the MP4 for every size that can be a video
(stories, posts, LED and mall screens), at the exact size and length,
with the delivery name. Two ways, picked at the top of the tab:

  - "Bring your statics to life": your exported pictures move (a slow
    camera push, your logo and promo text coming in), with Figma's
    motion words: Gentle, Quick, Bouncy, Slow, Dissolve, Slide in...
  - "Fit a Higgsfield video": one video from Higgsfield, cut to every
    size around the box you draw.

A preview plays every size before anything is made. The videos are made
with Concat, a free video editor you install yourself
(concatenate.pages.dev). Studio Helper doesn't include it.


CHATGPT
-------
If you use the ChatGPT desktop app, Studio Helper adds itself to
ChatGPT's MCP servers (with its skill) every time it starts, so it keeps
working after updates. Quit and reopen ChatGPT once to see it. ChatGPT
sees job names, sizes and statuses, never your artwork, and can't delete
anything. Turn it off in Settings -> ChatGPT.


ONE-TIME FIGMA SETUP
----------------------
If you use Figma for digital work:

  1. In Studio Helper, open ? -> Setup check and click the button in
     the Figma section. It opens the folder the plugin lives in.
  2. Open Figma desktop.
  3. Go to Plugins -> Development -> Import plugin from manifest...
  4. Pick manifest.json in the folder from step 1.

You only need to do this once. Updates keep the plugin in that same
folder, so Figma keeps finding it.


IF ILLUSTRATOR AUTOMATION FAILS
----------------------------------
Sometimes Illustrator won't let Studio Helper control it directly
(a permissions issue, or it's busy). When that happens, use the
manual path instead - Studio Helper will show you these same steps
on screen:

  1. In Studio Helper, click "Open scripts folder".
  2. In Illustrator: File -> Scripts -> Other Script...
  3. Pick the .jsx file Studio Helper told you to run.
  4. When it asks, select the job.json file for your job.

Everything still gets checked and named correctly - only the "click
one button in the browser" part is skipped.


UPDATING
---------
Easiest: click "?" at the top right, then "Check for updates", then
"Download & install" if one is available. Studio Helper downloads the new
version from GitHub, verifies it, and restarts itself into it - no
browser, no manual zip/unzip. This is the only thing in Studio Helper
that ever goes out to the internet, and only when you click it.

Manual alternative: extract the new zip (anywhere) and start it from
there. Your jobs, settings and job history are kept safely in your
Windows user profile and are not affected by updating either way.

Don't save your own files inside the Studio Helper folder. Old
versions' folders are cleaned up after an update; one that has your
files in it is left alone, but it's simpler to keep them elsewhere.


YOUR OPEN FILES ARE SAFE
--------------------------
You can keep your Illustrator or Photoshop file open while you use
Studio Helper. "Check only" never saves or closes it. Export saves
your unsaved changes first, then exports, and leaves the file open.


QUESTIONS OR SOMETHING LOOKS WRONG
-------------------------------------
Take a screenshot of the message Studio Helper shows (error messages
include the script name and line, which is enough to find the
problem), and send it along with the job's name.
